# The brace-expansion DoS advisories (GHSA-q2hr-2g5m-vwhr / GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7 /
# GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p) came from a copy bundled inside aws-cdk-lib's minimatch,
# which npm overrides cannot reach. Fixed in aws-cdk-lib 2.273.0.
#
# The sprintf-js advisory (GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c) in the dev-only Jest coverage
# chain is handled by the "overrides" entry in package.json, which moves
# @istanbuljs/load-nyc-config to js-yaml 4 (no argparse@1 / sprintf-js).
# Remove that override once @istanbuljs/load-nyc-config depends on js-yaml 4.
#
# Two advisories currently have no fix, so `npm audit` fails at its default level:
#   - GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4 (low): deepmerge <= 4.3.1 has no patched release. Dev-only,
#     reached through jest-config (jest, ts-jest).
#   - GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (moderate): the minimatch copy bundled inside aws-cdk-lib
#     2.275.0, which overrides cannot reach. Needs a new aws-cdk-lib release.
# The gate is therefore raised to "high" so that low and moderate findings no longer
# fail CI, while high and critical ones still do.
# Remove the audit-level line (back to the default) once both are fixed upstream.
audit-level=high
